      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "ArrayList vs LinkedList",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. ArrayList: a resizable array",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==ArrayList== is a resizable `Object[]`",
                "`get(i)` is {green:O(1)}; add at end is ==amortized O(1)==",
                "Insert/remove in the middle is {red:O(n)}: elements shift",
                "Grows by ~==1.5x== when full; pass an initial capacity if the size is known"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. LinkedList and the comparison",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==LinkedList== is a **doubly linked list**: each node holds prev and next",
                "`get(i)` is {red:O(n)}: walk the nodes",
                "Add/remove at either end or at a known node is {green:O(1)}",
                "Rarely faster in practice: per-node overhead, poor cache locality"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "ArrayList",
                "LinkedList"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`get(i)`",
                  "O(1)",
                  "O(n)"
                ],
                [
                  "Add at end",
                  "amortized O(1)",
                  "O(1)"
                ],
                [
                  "Insert in middle",
                  "O(n) shift",
                  "O(1) at known node"
                ],
                [
                  "Memory",
                  "compact, cache-friendly",
                  "node overhead"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistake: remove(int) vs remove(Object)",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "List<Integer> a = new ArrayList<>(List.of(10, 20, 1));",
                "a.remove(1);",
                "System.out.println(a);",
                "a.remove(Integer.valueOf(1));",
                "System.out.println(a);"
              ],
              "note": "remove(1) is an index, not a value"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "[10, 1]",
